/-
Shared definitions of the proofs of the lab's models of `google.golang.org/grpc` and
`google.golang.org/protobuf` (`harness/rpcmodel/grpc`, `harness/rpcmodel/protobuf`;
`notes/grpc-model.md`): the package-initialized state of each translated package.

* `protobuf/reflect/protoreflect`, `protobuf/runtime/protoimpl`, `grpc/codes`, `grpc/status`,
  `grpc/credentials`, `grpc/credentials/insecure`: no state a spec needs (`True`; `protoimpl`'s
  `X` is allocated and never read by translated code: every generated function that reads it is
  names only).
* `protobuf/proto`: `codecMu` is a mutex guarding `codec` (`codecInv`): `codec` is nil (owned),
  or a non-nil `*Codec` for good (`↦□`: the first `SetCodec` wins) whose fields hold the kit's
  codec functions for good (`codecFns`: `pbMarshal` and `pbUnmarshal`, which kitgen generates
  into the kit's package `PbKit.pkg`). The kit is a type class (`PbKit`), its instance generated
  into the kit's goal, so every `SetCodec` of a proved program registers the same functions.
* `grpc`: `errFrame` and `errNoTransportSecurity` hold their `errors.New` errors.
-/
module

public import Harness.GeneratedProof.google_golang_org.grpc
public import Harness.GeneratedProof.google_golang_org.protobuf.runtime.protoimpl
public import Harness.GeneratedProof.google_golang_org.grpc.credentials.insecure
public import Harness.Proof.net.Base
public import Perennial.Proof.context
public import Perennial.Spec.fmt.Sprintf

@[expose] public section

